getopts
Usage: getopts OPTSTRING NAME

Parse option flags in a shell script, one per call, in a loop. A letter
followed by : in OPTSTRING takes an argument, which lands in $OPTARG.
$OPTIND tracks how far along it got.

	while getopts "vf:" o; do
		case $o in
		v) verbose=1 ;;
		f) file=$OPTARG ;;
		esac
	done
	shift $((OPTIND - 1))

The trailing shift is what leaves the non-option arguments in "$@".

See also: shift, set, sh
